# .pen sources are plain UTF-8 JSON, not encrypted — anyone who clones this repo
# can read every board with `cat`. They are marked for how Pencil WRITES them,
# not for what they hold: `binary` also means `-merge`, and a three-way textual
# merge of two saves can land a document Pencil will not reopen. What changes on
# a save is coordinates and ids, so the review happens against the PNG exports
# beside them, which stay diffable.
designs/*.pen binary -diff
